		<title>Corkboard 7.1.2 Security Release</title>
		<link>https://news.corkboard.example/2026/09/corkboard-7-1-2-security-release/</link>
		
		<dc:creator><![CDATA[Odile Varga]]></dc:creator>
		<pubDate>Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:01:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<category><![CDATA[Releases]]></category>
		<category><![CDATA[Security]]></category>
		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.corkboard.example/?p=21731</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[This security release fixes one critical issue. Update your boards today, or let automatic updates do it for you, [&#8230;]]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">This security release fixes one critical issue.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Because this is a security release, update your boards today.</strong></p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What changed</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">A pinned note could include a file from the server under rare conditions. Thanks to <a href="https://security.example/">Henrik Solvang</a> for reporting it privately.</p>



<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Pinned notes check the files they include.</li>



<li>Uploads keep their original names out of the page.</li>
</ul>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
		<post-id xmlns="com-wordpress:feed-additions:1">21731</post-id>	</item>
